<title>UK: Rolls-Royce up on Boeing's FAA approval.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce up on Boeing's FAA approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in aero-engine maker Rolls-Royce rebounded on Friday from a week-long decline after Boeing Co said the U.S. Federal Aviation Administration granted initial approval to one of its airliners powered by Rolls-Royce engines.</p>
<p>AT 0815 GMT, Rolls-Royce shares were up 6-1/2p to 254p on volume of 3.4 million shares, the most actively traded stocks in London this morning.</p>
<p>Boeing said the U.S. FAA gave extended-range twin-engine operations approval to Boeing 777 airliners. The approval acknowledges the engine and aircraft design is reliable for ETOPS qualification.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
